            "id": "msg_1788354146666",
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "Zaroor shantanu sir! Yeh raha ek simple aur cute sa HTML, CSS aur JavaScript calculator ka code aapke liye:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>My Calculator</title>\n    <style>\n        body { display: flex; justify-content: center; padding-top: 50px; font-family: sans-serif; }\n        .calc { border: 2px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; }\n        input { width: 100%; height: 40px; margin-bottom: 10px; text-align: right; font-size: 20px; }\n        button { width: 45px; height: 45px; margin: 2px; cursor: pointer; }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"calc\">\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"display\" disabled>\n    <div>\n        <button onclick=\"clearDisplay()\">C</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('/')\">/</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('*')\">*</button>\n        <button onclick=\"deleteLast()\">DEL</button>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('7')\">7</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('8')\">8</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('9')\">9</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('-')\">-</button>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('4')\">4</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('5')\">5</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('6')\">6</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('+')\">+</button>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('1')\">1</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('2')\">2</button>\n        <button onclick=\"appendToDisplay('3')\">3</button>\n        <button onclick=\"calculate()\">=</button>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n    const display = document.getElementById('display');\n    function appendToDisplay(val) { display.value += val; }\n    function clearDisplay() { display.value = ''; }\n    function deleteLast() { display.value = display.value.slice(0, -1); }\n    function calculate() { try { display.value = eval(display.value); } catch { display.value = 'Error'; } }\n</script>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nUmeed hai shantanu sir, yeh aapke kaam aayega! Agar kuch aur badlav chahiye ho toh bas bata dijiye ga. 😊",
